---
title: Coaching packs
description: "Meal plan, recipe, question and card packs for coaches: what each file looks like and what card packs are given."
---

Four plugin kinds are for coaches. They show in Coaching › Plugins, next to workout blocks,
progression rules and program packs. A sport plugin is usually several of these together: the
climbing example in `plugins/first-party` is a Bouldering workout block, a "Climbing this week"
widget a coach puts on a client's Overview, and a question pack for their check-in form.

## Meal plan packs

Meal plans coaches copy into their own from Nutrition › Meal plans › Community. Pure JSON.

```json
{
  "formatVersion": 1,
  "pluginId": "com.you.cut-plans",
  "plans": [
    {
      "name": "High-protein cut, 1,900 kcal",
      "kcalTarget": 1900, "proteinG": 160,
      "meals": [
        { "id": "m1", "name": "Breakfast", "foods": [
          { "id": "f1", "name": "Greek yogurt, 0%", "grams": 300, "computed": { "kcal": 171, "proteinG": 30, "carbsG": 12, "fatG": 0 } }
        ] }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

Up to 20 plans, 10 meals each, 30 foods a meal. Each food needs a name, grams and its totals.

## Recipe packs

Recipes coaches copy from Nutrition › Recipes › From the community. Up to 100 recipes of up to 40
ingredients; per-serving totals are worked out from the ingredients.

```json
{
  "formatVersion": 1,
  "pluginId": "com.you.desserts",
  "recipes": [
    { "name": "Protein oats", "servings": 1, "tags": ["vegetarian"], "minutes": 5,
      "ingredients": [
        { "id": "i1", "name": "Rolled oats", "grams": 60, "computed": { "kcal": 228, "proteinG": 8, "carbsG": 39, "fatG": 4 } }
      ] }
  ]
}
```

## Question packs

Check-in questions a coach adds to a form (Add a question › From your plugins). Types:
`text` (with `long`), `number`, `scale` (`scaleMin`, `scaleMax`), `boolean`, `choice` (`options`,
`multi`), `weight`, `measurement` and `heading`. Up to 30 questions. Answers are the client's like
any other question's; the pack reads nothing.

```json
{
  "formatVersion": 1,
  "pluginId": "com.you.climbing-checkin",
  "questions": [
    { "prompt": "Finger pain", "type": "scale", "scaleMin": 1, "scaleMax": 10, "help": "1 = none, 10 = stop climbing" },
    { "prompt": "Skin", "type": "choice", "options": ["Fine", "Thin", "Split"] }
  ]
}
```

## Card packs

Code: one plugin with several cards for a coach's Today and Your month (Edit cards › Add a card).
`compute(input)` is called once per card and returns a [card view](/docs/plugins/primitives), like
a widget's.

```js
export const cards = {
  id: "com.you.roster",
  name: "Studio roster",
  cards: [{ id: "roster", name: "Months with you" }],
  compute(input) { /* input.card is "roster" */ },
};
```

`input` is `{ card, page, now, clients }`, and each client is only:
`firstName`, `monthsWithYou`, `joinedThisMonth`, `checkinsToReview`, and, for clients who share
workouts, `sessions7d` and `program` (`name`, `week`, `totalWeeks`, `endsInDays`). Never payments,
messages, food, weight or photos.

## Cards on a client's page

Any [widget](/docs/plugins/widgets) can be a card on a client's Overview (+ Card) and beside their
check-in. It gets the data slices it declares, from that client, and only those they share; up to
the end of the week, month or block the coach is looking at. Workouts include plugin blocks as
`blocks: [{ pluginId, name, fields, entries }]`, so a climbing card can read grades and sends.
